WEBVTT

00:00:08,850 --> 00:00:14,050
What is the CA-125 blood test?

00:00:14,050 --> 00:00:20,650
So a CA-125 blood test is a tumor marker test.

00:00:20,650 --> 00:00:26,250
I have a whole blog on tumor marker tests and what they mean.

00:00:26,250 --> 00:00:32,450
Tumor marker tests were developed decades ago.

00:00:32,450 --> 00:00:36,450
And it was in the hopes that that was going to be a great marker

00:00:36,450 --> 00:00:41,050
for monetary to person's cancer, either the progression,

00:00:41,050 --> 00:00:46,050
in a good way or a bad way through the treatment plan.

00:00:46,050 --> 00:00:49,450
They are tests that are a measuring different proteins.

00:00:49,450 --> 00:00:53,050
So they're normally found in a person's body,

00:00:53,050 --> 00:00:56,350
but they can be expressed at a greater amount

00:00:56,350 --> 00:00:57,850
if a person has cancer.

00:00:57,850 --> 00:01:02,050
And if the cancer is growing and getting worse,

00:01:02,050 --> 00:01:05,650
those tumor marker proteins can go up.

00:01:05,650 --> 00:01:08,550
Now, there are a number of these tumor markers

00:01:08,550 --> 00:01:10,450
that have been discovered.

00:01:10,450 --> 00:01:15,550
Now, the truth is that they're not super accurate

00:01:15,550 --> 00:01:19,050
as far as using them as objective data

00:01:19,050 --> 00:01:22,750
to see whether the person is getting better or getting worse.

00:01:22,750 --> 00:01:27,150
And if the person is undergoing chemotherapy,

00:01:27,150 --> 00:01:30,550
it can make them even less accurate.

00:01:30,550 --> 00:01:33,450
Because if a person's tumor is breaking up

00:01:33,550 --> 00:01:37,050
and dying quickly, it can spill out a lot more

00:01:37,050 --> 00:01:39,250
of these proteins in a person's tumor markers

00:01:39,250 --> 00:01:42,550
can actually be elevated and give them a false sense

00:01:42,550 --> 00:01:44,750
that they're getting worse when they're actually getting better.

00:01:44,750 --> 00:01:50,150
So a lot of oncologists ceased using tumor marker tests

00:01:50,150 --> 00:01:52,050
because of that, because they'd have to explain

00:01:52,050 --> 00:01:56,150
to the patient that it's not a very accurate test.

00:01:56,150 --> 00:01:57,550
Well, then why are you running it?

00:01:57,550 --> 00:01:59,450
When I'm doing chemo, when they're explaining,

00:01:59,450 --> 00:02:00,650
well, when you're doing chemo,

00:02:00,650 --> 00:02:02,450
then these aren't really accurate tests.

00:02:03,050 --> 00:02:04,550
It just gets very confusing.

00:02:04,550 --> 00:02:06,650
So they've kind of fallen out of use.

00:02:06,650 --> 00:02:11,450
But for a person who is wanting to monitor their cancer

00:02:12,450 --> 00:02:17,450
in a less invasive way,

00:02:17,450 --> 00:02:19,450
because they don't want to go and get another CT scanner.

00:02:19,450 --> 00:02:21,050
They don't want to go and get another PET scanner.

00:02:21,050 --> 00:02:22,750
They don't want to do those quite so often

00:02:22,750 --> 00:02:25,250
because that involves radiation or an MRI.

00:02:25,250 --> 00:02:30,050
They involve gadolidium or something

00:02:30,050 --> 00:02:33,950
that can be potentially dangerous to the person's body.

00:02:35,150 --> 00:02:37,350
We could do tumor marker blood tests

00:02:37,350 --> 00:02:39,750
so you could get those run.

00:02:39,750 --> 00:02:42,750
Now the pros and cons of them are,

00:02:42,750 --> 00:02:44,350
they can bounce around a little bit.

00:02:44,350 --> 00:02:46,650
It's not a perfect objective data.

00:02:46,650 --> 00:02:50,550
But the truth is, if you've heard me talk about

00:02:50,550 --> 00:02:53,450
any objective data, no objective data is perfect.

00:02:53,450 --> 00:02:57,150
Even a gold standard PET scan isn't perfect.

00:02:57,150 --> 00:03:00,950
Gold standard CT scan can be picking up swelling

00:03:00,950 --> 00:03:04,050
around a cancer that is not actually growth.

00:03:04,050 --> 00:03:06,750
It's actually in a inflammatory process

00:03:06,750 --> 00:03:08,950
that the cancer has died.

00:03:08,950 --> 00:03:11,550
So you have to take any objective test,

00:03:11,550 --> 00:03:13,350
any test that you got to weigh it

00:03:13,350 --> 00:03:15,050
with other tests that you're doing

00:03:15,050 --> 00:03:17,550
and subject of findings to really

00:03:17,550 --> 00:03:19,350
know whether the person is getting better

00:03:19,350 --> 00:03:21,950
or getting worse at the progression of care.

00:03:21,950 --> 00:03:25,350
So there's pros and cons to it.

00:03:25,350 --> 00:03:29,150
But what are the pros of doing tumor marker tests

00:03:29,150 --> 00:03:33,650
that is the fact that it isn't invasive?

00:03:33,650 --> 00:03:38,950
So the non-invasiveness of doing tumor marker tests

00:03:38,950 --> 00:03:43,050
can be super beneficial for a person

00:03:43,050 --> 00:03:45,050
who doesn't want to go over to a PET scan

00:03:45,050 --> 00:03:47,550
or a CT scan or something like that.

00:03:47,550 --> 00:03:50,150
Now the other problem with them is

00:03:50,150 --> 00:03:54,150
that some people will have a cancer

00:03:54,150 --> 00:03:55,750
that doesn't show tumor markers.

00:03:55,750 --> 00:04:00,150
So the thing to do is to run the test

00:04:00,150 --> 00:04:03,850
relatively soon in your care plan.

00:04:03,850 --> 00:04:07,050
So you know that where your baseline is.

00:04:07,050 --> 00:04:11,450
So in our Rupa lab store,

00:04:11,450 --> 00:04:12,950
we have a male tumor marker panel

00:04:12,950 --> 00:04:14,650
and an email term marker panel

00:04:14,650 --> 00:04:19,750
that tests for I think five or six tumor marker labs.

00:04:19,750 --> 00:04:22,150
And then it's relatively inexpensive.

00:04:22,150 --> 00:04:24,050
I think there are only about 90 bucks or something like that.

00:04:24,150 --> 00:04:26,150
To run a tumor marker panel.

00:04:26,150 --> 00:04:27,850
But at least you could know that you have

00:04:27,850 --> 00:04:30,950
kind of a baseline of whether you even

00:04:30,950 --> 00:04:34,350
show tumor markers or not.

00:04:34,350 --> 00:04:36,850
And that gives you an idea of whether

00:04:36,850 --> 00:04:38,650
that's going to be a good objective test for you

00:04:38,650 --> 00:04:43,250
to continue to run it on a regular basis to see how you're doing.

00:04:43,250 --> 00:04:47,750
But that's CA 125 is just one of those

00:04:47,750 --> 00:04:52,750
tumor marker tests that you could look at.

00:04:52,750 --> 00:04:57,720
So you can send it more questions

00:04:57,720 --> 00:04:59,720
on the chat history of that.

